BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 665 Tm (What happened:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 648 Tm (- Raw wrapped angle observations were unsuitable for global swing-up because of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 635 Tm (  the wrap discontinuity.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 622 Tm (- Switching to sin/cos angle observations was a major improvement.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 609 Tm (- The later unsigned arc-distance observation reduced dimension, but removed) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 596 Tm (  too much direction information and failed badly.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 579 Tm (Lesson:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 562 Tm (Compact observations are useful only if they preserve the information needed) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 551 Tm (to choose the control direction.) Tj ET
