BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 790 Tm (- The 500 Hz policy was trained with a 4 A current scale.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 777 Tm (- On hardware, full authority caused more strain and jitter.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 764 Tm (- Scaling to `0.4 * CurrentScale` gave more stable hardware operation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 747 Tm (Lesson:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 730 Tm (If a hardware limiter or scale factor changes the behavior, it should be) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 719 Tm (documented and eventually mirrored in training/evaluation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 697 Tm (9. Fine-Tuning Can Destroy A Working Policy) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 678 Tm (What happened:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 661 Tm (- Near-upright detailed-model fine-tuning from the old `500Hz_long` agent) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 648 Tm (  initially improved, then collapsed around episodes `46-55`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 635 Tm (- A smoke test suggested that loaded agent options/exploration/warm-start) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 622 Tm (  needed to be reapplied carefully.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 605 Tm (Lesson:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 588 Tm (When adapting a working policy, use gentle updates, low exploration, clear) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 577 Tm (option overrides, and possibly policy-preserving regularization.) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 555 Tm (10. Do Not Add Domain Randomization Too Early) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 536 Tm (What happened:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 519 Tm (- After hardware mismatch was observed, domain randomization looked attractive.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 506 Tm (- Detailed-model training then showed the nominal detailed model still did not) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 493 Tm (  learn clean capture/balance.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 476 Tm (Lesson:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 459 Tm (Randomizing a nominal model that cannot solve the task just makes a harder) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 448 Tm (unsolved task.) Tj ET
BT /F1 15 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 426 Tm (Detailed Mistakes And What We Learned) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 396 Tm (Mistake 1 - Early DDPG Was Pushed Too Long) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 377 Tm (What failed:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 360 Tm (- DDPG did not reliably learn local upright stabilization.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 347 Tm (- It produced high-frequency oscillatory torque around `125 Hz`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 334 Tm (- Fixed post-stage cases kept failing.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 317 Tm (What we learned:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 300 Tm (- The plant and sampled controller path were controllable, because the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 287 Tm (  classical/state-space controller could stabilize small errors.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 274 Tm (- The DDPG actor/critic training was too fragile for this delayed, saturated,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 261 Tm (  unstable system.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 248 Tm (- TD3 was a better next step because it changed fewer assumptions than SAC) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 235 Tm (  while addressing DDPG overestimation and unstable policy updates.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 218 Tm (Do:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 201 Tm (- Move on when a method repeatedly fails controlled diagnostics.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 184 Tm (Do not:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 167 Tm (- Keep retuning DDPG blindly when the algorithmic failure mode is visible.) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 143 Tm (Mistake 2 - Early Reward Could Prefer Quick Failure Or Weak Survival) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 124 Tm (What failed:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 107 Tm (- The original reward could make quick failure less costly than a longer,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 94 Tm (  unstable survival attempt.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 81 Tm (- Later, survival/alive reward could dominate fine behavior and allow) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 68 Tm (  continuous swinging.) Tj ET
endstream
