BT /F1 15 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 552 Tm (Why We Did Not Use The Brian Douglas Hybrid SAC/PPO Architecture) Tj ET
BT /F1 15 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 533 Tm (Directly) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 510 Tm (The Brian Douglas / MathWorks QUBE Servo2 reference in `references/` uses a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 497 Tm (hybrid architecture:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 480 Tm (classical feedback controller: upright balance) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 469 Tm (SAC agent: swing-up behavior / reference) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 458 Tm (PPO agent: mode selection between swing-up and balance) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 443 Tm (The reference also runs the RL agents more slowly than many of our early tests:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 426 Tm (feedback control period Tc = 0.005 s  -> 200 Hz) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 415 Tm (RL sample time Ts = Tc * 4 = 0.020 s  -> 50 Hz) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 404 Tm (episode length Tf = 10 s) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 393 Tm (RL steps per episode = 500) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 378 Tm (Why this architecture is attractive:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 361 Tm (- classical control handles the region where linearization works well,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 348 Tm (- RL only needs to learn the nonlinear swing-up part or switching logic,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 335 Tm (- the mode selector separates "when to swing" from "when to balance",) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 322 Tm (- it is closer to a practical supervised/hybrid controller than pure end-to-end) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 309 Tm (  RL.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 292 Tm (Why we did not follow it directly:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 275 Tm (1. Different project question.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 258 Tm (   This project intentionally tested a direct learned controller for the Furuta) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 245 Tm (   model. Using classical control for balance from the beginning would have made) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 232 Tm (   the result more like RL-assisted switching and less like direct RL control.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 215 Tm (2. Integration cost.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 198 Tm (   The Brian Douglas example targets the Quanser QUBE/Raspberry Pi workflow.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 185 Tm (   Our setup has the ZHAW Furuta model, SLDRT, UART, a microcontroller current) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 172 Tm (   PI loop, and different hardware signal conventions. Porting the full hybrid) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 159 Tm (   architecture would have added a large second integration project.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 142 Tm (3. Debugging complexity.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 125 Tm (   The hybrid system has three controllers to debug: SAC swing-up, PPO mode) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 112 Tm (   selector, and classical balance controller. Early on, we were still finding) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 99 Tm (   issues in reward scale, action scaling, sample time, observations, logging,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 86 Tm (   active plant choice, and hardware communication. Direct TD3 gave a cleaner) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 73 Tm (   baseline.) Tj ET
endstream
