BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 790 Tm (4. Controlled algorithm progression.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 773 Tm (   We started from DDPG. TD3 was the closest next step because it keeps the same) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 760 Tm (   deterministic continuous-action actor but fixes major DDPG weaknesses with) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 747 Tm (   twin critics, delayed actor updates, and target smoothing. SAC/PPO would have) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 734 Tm (   changed more assumptions at once.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 717 Tm (What we learned from it anyway:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 700 Tm (- The hybrid reference strongly supports using sin/cos angle observations.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 687 Tm (- It supports slower RL rates with a faster low-level controller underneath.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 674 Tm (- It shows that swing-up and balance can be separated into different control) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 661 Tm (  tasks.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 648 Tm (- It remains a good future architecture if direct TD3 capture stays brittle.) Tj ET
BT /F1 15 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 624 Tm (DDPG vs TD3 vs SAC vs PPO) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 594 Tm (DDPG) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 575 Tm (DDPG is an off-policy actor-critic method for continuous action spaces.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 558 Tm (In plain language:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 541 Tm (actor: maps observation -> deterministic action) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 530 Tm (critic: estimates Q\(observation, action\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 519 Tm (replay buffer: reuses old transitions for learning) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 504 Tm (Why it was attractive:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 487 Tm (- one continuous motor command,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 474 Tm (- actor can be deployed directly,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 461 Tm (- simpler than SAC/PPO hybrid architectures.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 444 Tm (What happened here:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 427 Tm (- DDPG did not reliably learn local upright stabilization,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 414 Tm (- fixed post-stage cases failed,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 401 Tm (- the actor produced high-frequency oscillatory torque,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 388 Tm (- the method was too fragile for our delayed, saturated, unstable setup.) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 364 Tm (TD3) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 345 Tm (TD3 is essentially a stronger DDPG-family method.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 328 Tm (Key changes:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 311 Tm (- two critics reduce over-optimistic Q estimates,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 298 Tm (- actor updates are delayed relative to critic updates,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 285 Tm (- target action smoothing discourages brittle sharp Q peaks.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 268 Tm (Why it became our main method:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 251 Tm (- still gives a deterministic actor for deployment,) Tj ET
